{"availability":"available","full":"Jagadeeshftw/memokit","name":"memokit","description":"XRPL-originated calls on assets a Flare account already holds. No FAssets mint in the path, no Flare-assigned destination tag or wallet registration.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-22T08:56:11Z","updated":"2026-10-01T11:49:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://memokit.0xo.in/docs/introduction","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T16:19:52.817Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T16:19:52.817Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T16:19:52.817Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T16:19:52.817Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"x","name":"As Seen On X.com","url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2105682213295776252","postId":"2105682213295776252","postedAt":"2026-10-01T15:32:15.000Z"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T21:45:31.260Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-12T16:19:52.817Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["memokit executes XRPL-originated calls on assets a Flare account already holds. memokit never mints FXRP to do it, there is no destination tag, and no wallet registration.","You sign one XRPL Payment. Its memo is either a 42-byte commitment to what your Flare account should do, or the instruction itself, inline. FDC attests the payment, anyone submits the proof, and the account runs exactly the calls you committed to: a vault deposit, a payout to five addresses, a borrow, a swap — or a redemption that sends XRP back to your own XRPL address. You never hold an EVM key at any point.","Flare Smart Accounts already reaches arbitrary calls through memo opcodes 0xFF/0xFE, but only as a side effect of FAssets direct minting (verified from Flare's deployed contracts, 2026-09-30; see CLAIMS.md): every such instruction mints FXRP and inherits FAssets' direct-minting limits. Without a mint it offers a fixed menu of instructions: transfer FXRP, redeem it, and deposit into or withdraw from registered vaults. That coupling is the gap memokit fills. The account is derived from your XRPL address alone, so there is nothing to register and no tag to buy."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jagadeeshftw/memokit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"aac9c02e82c35363f46efb72f6caa24b94ec439111fdec4f29d137bbd97e425c","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T21:45:31.260Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T16:19:52.817Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"memokit executes XRPL-originated calls on assets a Flare account already holds. memokit never mints FXRP to do it, there is no destination tag, and no wallet registration.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jagadeeshftw/memokit/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"A payload-format change needs a redeploy, and a redeploy moves every account address.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jagadeeshftw/memokit/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"aac9c02e82c35363f46efb72f6caa24b94ec439111fdec4f29d137bbd97e425c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jagadeeshftw/memokit/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T16:19:52.817Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-01T11:49:50Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jagadeeshftw/memokit/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T16:19:52.817Z","hash":"aac9c02e82c35363f46efb72f6caa24b94ec439111fdec4f29d137bbd97e425c","originalBytes":24923,"storedBytes":24923,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["executor","run","xrpl","flare","live","memokit","payment","instruction","one","account","execute","every","fee","npm","xrp","fork","fxrp","payload","proof","attestation","fdc","fixtures","agent","coston2","measurements","paid","payout","round","see","what","after","against","cash-out","fassets","five","ftestxrp","ledger","address","because","block","mainnet","memo","never","rather","sdk","only","out","phase2.md","phase3.md","